Corrected message:

Replace shape and text tool key-binding if-chains with tables

No behavior change.

Shape tools: the configured-binding checks become one ordered
binding-to-command table, and a single command switch runs both those
bindings and the default-key fallback.

Text tool: the 17 configured-binding checks become one ordered table
and switch, and font size up/down share one handler across the binding
and fallback paths. The rest of the default-key fallback is left
separate, because several of its keys behave differently from the
binding path (they read live Ctrl/Shift state, or skip the final
redraw).

Adds tests that each table lists every command exactly once and that
each binding's gesture on a fresh profile equals its default.
